Adopt native Codex daemons from mbid/main

Install complete Codex packages so bundled tools and resources remain
discoverable, and use Codex 0.163 in prepared images and development
tests.

Let Codex manage its daemon over a Unix socket, restore activated pods
on startup, and retain pod entry when daemon restoration fails. Preserve
pod-owned credentials and permission settings across reconnects, and
keep conversation snapshots consistent without cloning runtime state or
remote control identities into forked pods.

Keep the existing 128 MiB WebSocket limits across the native transport
so large plugin catalogs continue to work after the daemon migration.
